'''bourrée''' (bö-rā′), ''n.'' [F.: see ''boree.''] '''1.''' A lively dance, originating either in Auvergne or in Biscay.—'''2.''' A musical composition in which the strict rhythm and cheerful character of such a dance are embodied. {{smaller|It is usually written in duple rhythm, the phrases being two measures long, beginning}}
